{
  "format": "call-of-slop-construct-part/1",
  "name": "Press",
  "description": "A Press Core, the press's power pack and control module: stamps parts out of extruded pieces under a swing lid. Alone it takes blanks up to 0.45 m across on its deck; weld Press Blocks beside it for a bed (along the flow from the Core; its width across the widest blank) and the press gets its lid: one heavy lid hinged on the frame across from the Core that swings shut on the blank, latches, squeezes and swings open, with a lower die whose jaws close to each blank's size. The bed's width sets the daylight (1.6 m for 2 or 3 blocks across, 2 m more a pair more); nothing stacks on the bed, and the strip beside the hinge side must be clear for the open lid. The top stays open, so a crane can drop a blank on the die, or a Roller Tile run rolls one onto a low bed. It works faster with every block. The lid never stops for anyone. A die in its slot sets what it makes; blanks go in bay 1, a die's kit in bay 2. Needs power.",
